msgid "架构差异分析"
msgstr "Architecture Difference Analysis"

msgid "本⽂系统性梳理两⼤平台的核⼼架构、编程规则与优化⼿段差异，拆解昇腾NPU Triton专属开发特性与适配要点，帮助开发者快速建⽴昇腾NPU Triton开发思维，精准完成算⼦迁移、代码适配与性能调优⼯作，规避迁移常⻅问题。"
msgstr "This document systematically reviews the differences in core architecture, programming rules, and optimization methods between the two major platforms. It breaks down the Ascend NPU Triton-specific development features and key adaptation points. This helps developers quickly establish an Ascend NPU Triton development mindset to accurately complete operator migration, code adaptation, and performance tuning, and to avoid common migration issues."

msgid "多核任务并行策略"
msgstr "Multi-core task parallel strategy"

msgid "NPU在Triton多核并行中是物理核强绑定模式，与GPU逻辑维度并行+硬件自动物理映射的模式形成核心差异，核心对比如下表所示："
msgstr "In Triton multi-core parallelism, the NPU uses a physical-core strong-binding mode. This differs fundamentally from the GPU, which uses logical dimension parallelism with automatic hardware physical mapping. The core comparison is shown in the following table:"

msgid "维度"
msgstr "Dimension"

msgid "GPU（NVIDIA）"
msgstr "GPU（NVIDIA）"

msgid "昇腾（Ascend）"
msgstr "Ascend"

msgid "grid 本质"
msgstr "The essence of grid"

msgid "逻辑任务维度（和物理核解耦）"
msgstr "Logical task dimension (decoupled from physical cores)"

msgid "物理核组映射（绑定 AI Core 拓扑）"
msgstr "Physical core group mapping (binding to the AI Core topology)"

msgid "核数 / 维度限制"
msgstr "Core Count / Dimension Limits"

msgid "grid 维度 / 大小无硬限制"
msgstr "grid dimensions / size have no hard limits"

msgid "grid 大小≤AI Core 总数，2D 需匹配拓扑"
msgstr "The grid size must be less than or equal to the total number of AI Cores, and the 2D grid must match the topology."

msgid "GPU可绑定多个维度轴（三维grid=[n,m,l] 等同于乘积n×m×l个并行线程），每个线程仅对应一次kernel执行，且仅执行一次。 NPU的Vector核、Cube核属于多个物理核，不同代际硬件核数不同，每个核仅执行一次Block,且支持对该Block重复调度执行。"
msgstr "A GPU can bind multiple dimension axes (a three-dimensional grid=[n,m,l] is equivalent to the product of n×m×l parallel threads). Each thread corresponds to only one kernel execution and executes only once. The Vector cores and Cube cores of the NPU are multiple physical cores. Different hardware generations have different numbers of cores. Each core executes a Block only once and supports repeated scheduling of that Block for execution."

