msgstr ""
"\\\\\n"

msgid "充分利用核数"
msgstr "Fully utilize the cores"

msgid "昇腾NPU具备多个计算核心，合理分配并充分利用所有可用核心，是提升算子性能的关键因素之一。 在调用Triton内核函数时，通过设置launch参数控制使用的核数量。以GELU算子为例："
msgstr "The Ascend NPU has multiple compute cores. Properly allocating and fully utilizing all available cores is one of the key factors for improving operator performance. When calling a Triton kernel, control the number of cores used by setting the launch parameter. Using the GELU operator as an example:"

msgid ""
"triton_gelu[n, 1, 1](...)  # 第一个参数表示使用的核数，n表示使用n个核\n"
msgstr ""
"triton_gelu[n, 1, 1](...)  # The first parameter indicates the number of cores used; n indicates that n cores are used\n"

msgid "通过对核数的调优，可实现对所有计算资源的充分调度和利用，从而最大化并行度与吞吐量。未启用 `auto-blockify`（见下节）时，启动grid的核数需小于等于 65,535。"
msgstr "By tuning the number of cores, you can fully schedule and utilize all computing resources to maximize parallelism and throughput. If you do not enable `auto-blockify` (see the next section), the number of cores used to launch the grid must be less than or equal to 65,535."

msgid "auto-blockify：突破 65,535 逻辑块上限"
msgstr "auto-blockify: Breaking through the 65,535 logical block limit"

msgid "社区 Triton 在 NVIDIA GPU 上把 grid 视为纯逻辑维度 —— `n` 个逻辑块按 1:1 映射到 `n` 个硬件块，运行时由硬件分发到各 SM，每个块不需要内部循环。昇腾上由于[多核任务并行策略](#多核任务并行策略)中描述的物理核强绑定，可启动的 grid 上限被限制在 65,535，对含百万级逻辑工作项的 kernel（autotune 后的 reduce/scan、megablocks 风格的稀疏 kernel 等）过于严苛。"
msgstr "Community Triton treats grid as a purely logical dimension on NVIDIA GPUs — `n` logical blocks are mapped 1:1 to `n` hardware blocks, the hardware dispatches them to each SM at runtime, and each block does not require internal loops. On Ascend, due to the physical core strong binding described in [Multi-core Task Parallel Strategy](#多核任务并行策略), the maximum number of launchable grids is limited to 65,535, which is overly restrictive for kernels with millions of logical work items (reduce/scan after autotune, megablocks-style sparse kernels, and so on)."

msgid "`auto-blockify`（`SIMTAutoBlockify` 编译期 pass + 配套的运行期 cap）通过\"编译期视为逻辑、启动期折叠到物理核\"消除该限制："
msgstr "`auto-blockify` (`SIMTAutoBlockify` compile-time pass + a matching runtime cap) eliminates this limitation by \"treating as logical at compile time and folding to physical cores at launch time\":"

msgid "**编译期**：Triton pass 把 kernel 函数体包进一层 `scf.for`，迭代变量由 `gpu.linear_block_id` 提供。chunk 大小 = `ceildiv(logical_block_count, physical_core_count)`，每个物理块依次跑 `chunk` 个逻辑 block id。"
msgstr "**Compile time**: A Triton pass wraps the kernel function body in an `scf.for` loop, and the iteration variable is provided by `gpu.linear_block_id`. The chunk size equals `ceildiv(logical_block_count, physical_core_count)`, and each physical block sequentially runs `chunk` logical block IDs."

msgid "**运行期**：传给 launcher 的 block-count 参数从逻辑 grid clamp 到 `physical_core_count`，与编译期的折叠保持一致。"
msgstr "**Runtime**: The `block-count` parameter passed to the launcher is clamped from the logical grid to `physical_core_count`, consistent with compile-time folding."

msgid "编译期和运行期共享同一份后端内部策略。自动 block mapping 由后端统一启用，编译器生成的 IR 安全标记会排除不适用的 kernel。因此，编译期循环包与运行期 cap 始终同步，不存在 kernel 按一种模式编译却按另一种模式启动的情形。"
msgstr "The compile time and runtime share the same backend internal policy. The automatic block mapping is uniformly enabled by the backend, and the IR safety markers generated by the compiler exclude inapplicable kernels. Therefore, the compile-time loop package and the runtime cap are always synchronized, and a kernel cannot be compiled in one mode but launched in another mode."

msgid "从 GPU Triton kernel 移植时的注意事项："
msgstr "Precautions when porting from a GPU Triton kernel:"

msgid "grid 大于 65,535 可直接运行，无需手动把外层维度折叠进 kernel 函数体。"
msgstr "A grid larger than 65,535 can run directly, without the need to manually fold the outer dimension into the kernel function body."

msgid "逻辑块之间必须保持顺序无关（循环按 chunk 顺序访问）。依赖严格逻辑 block id 顺序的 kernel（如基于特定顺序的跨块同步）需要改写。"
msgstr "Logical blocks must remain order-independent (loops access chunks in order). Kernels that depend on a strict logical block ID order (such as cross-block synchronization based on a specific order) must be rewritten."

msgid "per-block workspace 分配从 `O(logical_block_count)` 降到 `O(physical_core_count)`，因为 workspace 在内层 `scf.for` 各次迭代间复用。"
msgstr "The per-block workspace allocation decreases from `O(logical_block_count)` to `O(physical_core_count)` because the workspace is reused across iterations of the inner `scf.for`."

msgid "单核数据搬运策略"
msgstr "Single-Core Data Movement Strategy"

msgid "数据切分Tiling"
msgstr "Data Tiling"

msgid "写Triton内核函数时，合理的数据切分策略对性能优化至关重要。通过调整不同的切分粒度参数，可以在不同维度上平衡计算负载与内存访问效率。"
msgstr "When you write Triton kernel functions, a proper data tiling strategy is crucial for performance optimization. By adjusting different tiling granularity parameters, you can balance the computational load and memory access efficiency across different dimensions."

msgid "常见的切分参数包括："
msgstr "Common tiling parameters include:"

msgid ""
"ncore：使用的核数（跨核切分）\n"
"xblock：核间数据块大小（核间切分）\n"
"xblock_sub：核内切分粒度（核内细粒度划分）\n"
msgstr ""
"ncore: Number of cores used (cross-core tiling)\n"
"xblock: Inter-core data block size (inter-core tiling)\n"
"xblock_sub: Intra-core tiling granularity (fine-grained intra-core partitioning)\n"

msgid "开发者可根据实际场景手动选择最优的切分配置，使得每次计算尽可能充分利用片上内存（On-chip Memory），避免频繁访问全局内存（Global Memory）造成的 性能瓶颈。"
msgstr "You can manually select the optimal tiling configuration based on your scenario. This maximizes on-chip memory usage for each computation, avoiding performance bottlenecks caused by frequent global memory access."

msgid "以GELU算子为例，通过调整切分参数，可以有效适配片上缓存容量限制，从而提升执行效率。"
msgstr "Using the GELU operator as an example, adjusting the tiling parameters can effectively adapt to the on-chip cache capacity limit, thereby improving execution efficiency."

msgid "注：Atlas 800T A2训练服务器、Atlas 800I A2推理服务器的片上内存容量为192KB，因此在设计切分策略时需考虑该限制，确保每轮计算的数据量不超过片上内存容量。"
msgstr "Note: The on-chip memory capacity of the Atlas 800T A2 training server and Atlas 800I A2 inference server is 192 KB. Therefore, consider this limit when designing the tiling strategy to ensure that the data volume per computation round does not exceed the on-chip memory capacity."

msgid "GELU算子示例"
msgstr "GELU operator example"

msgid "GELU算子开发示例，使用3种方式计算结果。"
msgstr "The GELU operator development sample uses three methods to calculate the result."

msgid "standard_unary      为标准Torch计算。"
msgstr "standard_unary      is a standard Torch computation."

msgid "triton_easy_kernel  为简单Triton实现。"
msgstr "triton_easy_kernel  is a simple Triton implementation."

msgid "triton_better_kernel为更高效的Triton实现。"
msgstr "`triton_better_kernel` is a more efficient Triton implementation."

msgid "标准Torch写法"
msgstr "Standard Torch syntax"

msgid "输入tensor x0，经过torch计算实现 GELU 算子，返回结果值。"
msgstr "Input the tensor x0, implement the GELU operator using torch computation, and return the result value."

msgid ""
"def standard_unary(x0):\n"
"    res = x0 * 0.5 * (1.0 + torch.erf(x0 / torch.sqrt(torch.tensor(2.0))))\n"
"    return res\n"
msgstr ""
"def standard_unary(x0):\n"
"    res = x0 * 0.5 * (1.0 + torch.erf(x0 / torch.sqrt(torch.tensor(2.0))))\n"
"    return res\n"

msgid "简单Triton写法"
msgstr "Simple Triton Syntax"

msgid "以下是一个使用 Triton 编写的简单内核示例，用于展示如何定义和调用一个基本的Triton内核函数。此示例实现了一个简单的数学运算（GELU 激活函数）。"
msgstr "The following is a simple kernel sample written using Triton to demonstrate how to define and call a basic Triton kernel function. This sample implements a simple mathematical operation (GELU activation function)."

msgid ""
"\n"
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"\n"
"# 定义triton_kernel核函数\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def triton_easy_kernel(in_ptr0, out_ptr0, NUMEL: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    idx_block = tl.arange(0, NUMEL)\n"
"    x = tl.load(in_ptr0 + idx_block)\n"
"    ret = x * 0.5 * (1.0 + tl.erf(x / tl.sqrt(2.0)))\n"
"    tl.store(out_ptr0 + idx_block, ret)\n"
"\n"
"# 调用triton_kernel核函数\n"
"x0 = torch.rand(32768, device='npu')\n"
"out1 = torch.empty_like(x0)\n"
"triton_easy_kernel[1, 1, 1](x0, out1, x0.numel())\n"
msgstr ""
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"\n"
"# Define the triton_kernel kernel\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def triton_easy_kernel(in_ptr0, out_ptr0, NUMEL: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    idx_block = tl.arange(0, NUMEL)\n"
"    x = tl.load(in_ptr0 + idx_block)\n"
"    ret = x * 0.5 * (1.0 + tl.erf(x / tl.sqrt(2.0)))\n"
"    tl.store(out_ptr0 + idx_block, ret)\n"
"\n"
"# Call the triton_kernel kernel\n"
"x0 = torch.rand(32768, device='npu')\n"
"out1 = torch.empty_like(x0)\n"
"triton_easy_kernel[1, 1, 1](x0, out1, x0.numel())\n"

msgid "注意事项"
msgstr "Precautions"

msgid "内存限制：上述写法中，所有输入数据一次性被加载到内存中进行计算。如果输入张量过大，可能会超出单个内核的片上内存容量，导致内存溢出错误。 因此，这种简单的写法更适合于小规模张量的计算或用于理解 Triton 内核的基本写法和调用方式。"
msgstr "Memory limit: In the preceding approach, all input data is loaded into memory at once for computation. If the input tensor is too large, it may exceed the on-chip memory capacity of a single kernel, causing an out-of-memory error. Therefore, this simple approach is more suitable for small-scale tensor computation or for understanding the basic syntax and invocation methods of Triton kernels."

msgid "适用场景：尽管这种方法有助于快速理解和入门 Triton 编程，但对于大规模数据集或高性能要求的应用场景，建议采用更复杂的数据切分策略（如 Tiling）， 以充分利用硬件资源并避免内存溢出问题。通过这种方式，开发者可以快速上手 Triton 编程，同时了解如何定义、调用以及优化 Triton 内核函数。"
msgstr "Applicable scenarios: Although this method helps you quickly understand and get started with Triton programming, for large-scale datasets or high-performance scenarios, we recommend a more complex data tiling strategy (such as Tiling). This strategy fully utilizes hardware resources and avoids out-of-memory issues. In this way, developers can quickly get started with Triton programming and understand how to define, call, and optimize Triton kernel functions."

msgid "更高效triton写法"
msgstr "More efficient Triton writing methods"

msgid "在昇腾 NPU 上使用 Triton 编写高性能算子时，为了充分利用硬件资源、避免内存溢出并提升执行效率，通常需要采用数据切分（Tiling）策略。 下面是一个经过优化的 Triton 内核实现示例，适用于大规模张量计算。"
msgstr "When you write high-performance operators using Triton on an Ascend NPU, you typically need to adopt a data tiling strategy. This strategy fully utilizes hardware resources, avoids memory overflow, and improves execution efficiency. The following optimized Triton kernel implementation sample is suitable for large-scale tensor computation."

msgid ""
"\n"
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"\n"
"# 定义triton_kernel核函数\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def triton_better_kernel(in_ptr0, out_ptr0, xnumel, XBLOCK: tl.constexpr, XBLOCK_SUB: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    xoffset = tl.program_id(0) * XBLOCK\n"
"    for xoffset_sub in range(0, XBLOCK, XBLOCK_SUB):\n"
"        x_index = xoffset + xoffset_sub + tl.arange(0, XBLOCK_SUB)[:]\n"
"        xmask = x_index < xnumel\n"
"        x = tl.load(in_ptr0 + x_index, xmask)\n"
"        ret = x * 0.5 * (1.0 + tl.erf(x / tl.sqrt(2.0)))\n"
"        tl.store(out_ptr0 + x_index, ret, xmask)\n"
"\n"
"ncore = 32\n"
"xblock = 32768\n"
"xblock_sub = 8192\n"
"x0 = torch.rand(32768, device='npu')\n"
"out1 = torch.empty_like(x0)\n"
"# 调用triton_kernel核函数\n"
"triton_better_kernel[ncore, 1, 1](x0, out1, x0.numel(), xblock, xblock_sub)\n"
msgstr ""
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"\n"
"# Define the triton_kernel kernel\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def triton_better_kernel(in_ptr0, out_ptr0, xnumel, XBLOCK: tl.constexpr, XBLOCK_SUB: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    xoffset = tl.program_id(0) * XBLOCK\n"
"    for xoffset_sub in range(0, XBLOCK, XBLOCK_SUB):\n"
"        x_index = xoffset + xoffset_sub + tl.arange(0, XBLOCK_SUB)[:]\n"
"        xmask = x_index < xnumel\n"
"        x = tl.load(in_ptr0 + x_index, xmask)\n"
"        ret = x * 0.5 * (1.0 + tl.erf(x / tl.sqrt(2.0)))\n"
"        tl.store(out_ptr0 + x_index, ret, xmask)\n"
"\n"
"ncore = 32\n"
"xblock = 32768\n"
"xblock_sub = 8192\n"
"x0 = torch.rand(32768, device='npu')\n"
"out1 = torch.empty_like(x0)\n"
"# Call the triton_kernel kernel\n"
"triton_better_kernel[ncore, 1, 1](x0, out1, x0.numel(), xblock, xblock_sub)\n"

msgid "关键代码解释"
msgstr "Key Code Explanation"

msgid ""
"# 计算当前核处理数据块的起始偏移地址，实现核间切分。每个核仅负责 XBLOCK 大小的数据范围。\n"
"xoffset = tl.program_id(0) * XBLOCK\n"
"\n"
"# 在单个核内部进一步细分数据块，每次处理 XBLOCK_SUB 大小的数据，实现核内切分。\n"
"for xoffset_sub in range(0, XBLOCK, XBLOCK_SUB):\n"
"\n"
"# 构造当前迭代的数据索引数组，用于访问输入和输出张量。\n"
"x_index = xoffset + xoffset_sub + tl.arange(0, XBLOCK_SUB)[:]\n"
"\n"
"# 设置掩码以防止越界访问，确保只处理合法范围内的数据。\n"
"xmask = x_index < xnumel\n"
"\n"
"# 分别用于从全局内存加载数据到片上内存，以及将计算结果写回全局内存。\n"
"tl.load() 和 tl.store()\n"
msgstr ""
"# Calculate the starting offset address of the data block processed by the current core to implement inter-core partitioning. Each core is responsible only for a data range of the XBLOCK size.\n"
"xoffset = tl.program_id(0) * XBLOCK\n"
"\n"
"# Further subdivide the data block within a single core, processing data of the XBLOCK_SUB size each time to implement intra-core partitioning.\n"
"for xoffset_sub in range(0, XBLOCK, XBLOCK_SUB):\n"
"\n"
"# Construct the data index array for the current iteration to access the input and output tensors.\n"
"x_index = xoffset + xoffset_sub + tl.arange(0, XBLOCK_SUB)[:]\n"
"\n"
"# Set a mask to prevent out-of-bounds access, ensuring that only data within the valid range is processed.\n"
"xmask = x_index < xnumel\n"
"\n"
"# Used to load data from the global memory to the on-chip memory and to write the computation results back to the global memory, respectively.\n"
"tl.load() and tl.store()\n"

